_exptl_crystal_grow.pdbx_details    
;PVAMA1 AND FAB-F8.12.19 WERE MIXED IN A 1:1 STOICHIOMETRIC RATIO AND LEFT TO INCUBATE FOR 4 HOURS AT ROOM TEMPERATURE TO FORM THE ANTIBODY-ANTIGEN COMPLEX BEFORE MIXING WITH CRYSTALLISATION SCREENING BUFFERS. CRYSTALS USED FOR DIFFRACTION MEASUREMENTS WERE OBTAINED AS FOLLOWS. THE CRYSTALLISATION BUFFER IN THE RESERVOIR COMPRISED 10% PEG 6000 AND 0.1 M SODIUM ACETATE BUFFERED TO PH 4.4. THE CRYSTALLISATION DROP WAS PREPARED BY ADDING 0.8 MICROLITRES OF THE CRYSTALLISATION BUFFER TO 0.8 MICROLITRES OF THE PVAMA1-FAB COMPLEX, GIVING A FINAL PROTEIN CONCENTRATION OF 3.9 MG/ML.
;
